#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccfebb3-3017-5639-8b67-058c304c9df8" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Binomial CDF Table"}] :question/id #uuid "56d68682-0e4d-57e5-9441-997cf4d33f29" :question/math-academy-id "e-15052" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X\\sim B(7, 0.63).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\displaystyle \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=7$ and $p=0.63.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n- For $F(6),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =0.7987+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6})(0.63)^{6}(1-0.63)^{7-6} \\\\  & =0.7987+7\\cdot (0.63)^{6}\\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9606.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Since $n=7,$ we have that $F(7) = P(X\\leq 7) = 1.$\n\nTherefore, our completed table looks as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.9606}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69c62fd8-05af-57dc-a96c-4dcba884ea32" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Using the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "92a73e93-f882-5329-a19c-00a6a270bced" :question/math-academy-id "e-15054" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.0969-0.0170 \\\\  & =0.0799\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f0c914d-f2c0-5641-9818-312eac10d1b4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Using the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "c80fb077-2d31-522b-8083-5a72613f84de" :question/math-academy-id "e-15055" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X<5) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X<5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<5) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.9163-0.0222 \\\\  & =0.8941.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95b5e3bd-0e7e-56df-80d5-be39de76da16" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "c9a6a708-925d-54aa-ac0a-023e5259d19a" :question/math-academy-id "e-15056" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(7, 0.52)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0504\\,$ | $\\,0.1951\\,$ | $\\,0.4563\\,$ | $\\,0.7393\\,$ | $\\,0.9233\\,$ | $\\,0.9897\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 2) = P(X \\gt 1).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X>1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-F(1) \\\\  & =1-0.0504 \\\\  & =0.9496.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccfebb3-3017-5639-8b67-058c304c9df8" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Binomial CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1642" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1642" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425528} :answer-field/id #uuid "b69d6c50-4593-518f-9ffd-5e85fb9bb8a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425524} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7f40b0-78f3-55c9-9c52-0b2466a01973" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2747e086-f93d-5020-86de-46c90085c6ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-224463" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.26.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6} \\\\  & ≈0.1642.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1})(0.26)^{1}(1-0.26)^{6-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6}+6\\cdot (0.26)^{1}\\cdot (0.74)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.5104.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccfebb3-3017-5639-8b67-058c304c9df8" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Binomial CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9246" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9246" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425521} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd714c02-0a09-5253-9229-c78cde01f445" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5" :question/math-academy-id "q-224505" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.65).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $0.0018$ | $0.0223$ | $0.1174$ | $0.3529$ | $0.6809$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.65.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =0.6809+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.65)^{5}(1-0.65)^{6-5} \\\\  & =0.6809+6\\cdot (0.65)^{5}\\cdot (0.35)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9246.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69c62fd8-05af-57dc-a96c-4dcba884ea32" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Using the CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45c1d3ae-7aea-5878-b0b0-750018287438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6794" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425518} {:answer/id #uuid "4d21eaac-b64d-59c5-a232-eec231b01fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0872" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425519} {:answer/id #uuid "d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0738" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425527} {:answer/id #uuid "dac293d3-2b8c-5f02-8569-0ff33e3f1998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2834" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425529} {:answer/id #uuid "f232fefc-778d-57b7-9c36-9f38d8b9078a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2096" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0738" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425527} :answer-field/id #uuid "a166156c-a351-5495-9912-8c241a9caedf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e" :question/math-academy-id "q-224517" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.85)$ given below, compute $P(X<5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0000\\,$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0012\\,$ | $\\,0.0121\\,$ | $\\,0.0738\\,$ | $\\,0.2834\\,$ | $\\,0.6794\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4) \\\\  & =0.0738.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69c62fd8-05af-57dc-a96c-4dcba884ea32" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Using the CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425530} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd2bd7d-81b6-570e-8fdd-b4fa401ea4d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-224526" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X=3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0198\\,$ | $\\,0.1293\\,$ | $\\,0.3820\\,$ | $\\,0.6930\\,$ | $\\,0.9083\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X=3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(X=3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6930-0.3820 \\\\  & =0.3110.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f0c914d-f2c0-5641-9818-312eac10d1b4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Using the CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425514} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53b86c5-f2cb-5dad-8677-36c6c80c81f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde" :question/math-academy-id "q-225123" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.63)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0069\\,$ | $\\,0.0660\\,$ | $\\,0.2670\\,$ | $\\,0.6093\\,$ | $\\,0.9008\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.2670 \\\\  & =0.7330.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f0c914d-f2c0-5641-9818-312eac10d1b4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Using the CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9011" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425513} {:answer/id #uuid "363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0989" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425515} {:answer/id #uuid "3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9984" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425516} {:answer/id #uuid "630e58a3-661e-52d8-a8d1-903e9b5e6179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0001" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425522} {:answer/id #uuid "c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9999" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9999" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425526} :answer-field/id #uuid "f954b4ca-ba90-55e4-8907-f07c9675da77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39452c92-9de3-5f42-bbde-2d7fa0b6b73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225125" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.8)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0016\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0989\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.7379\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(0) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.0001 \\\\  & =0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95b5e3bd-0e7e-56df-80d5-be39de76da16" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3077" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425517} {:answer/id #uuid "557c159a-30a2-562f-a119-f39d2d4ff550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6923" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425520} {:answer/id #uuid "65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7167" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425523} {:answer/id #uuid "aaaac3c2-cb51-55eb-b7b3-6b277435e640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9341" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425525} {:answer/id #uuid "f23fa1b7-310e-5e39-a994-088b046f6326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2833" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7167" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425523} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5be0410-2431-593a-bcce-244299805303" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527" :question/math-academy-id "q-225190" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.79)$ given below, compute $P(X>3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0004\\,$ | $\\,0.0081\\,$ | $\\,0.0659\\,$ | $\\,0.2833\\,$ | $\\,0.6923\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.2833 \\\\  & =0.7167.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95b5e3bd-0e7e-56df-80d5-be39de76da16" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0504" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0504" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425512} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d59258b-b2f8-5954-823d-22bfd5f84b58" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3dbd9a46-63be-542a-8056-c34929af9e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-225192" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0767\\,$ | $\\,0.2607\\,$ | $\\,0.5437\\,$ | $\\,0.8049\\,$ | $\\,0.9496\\,$ | $\\,0.9941\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9496 \\\\  & =0.0504.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
